## Clues

A1. Word (initialism, technically) added at the end of a text to soften it ~ LOL
A4. Surveys, like the lunchtime one in Heathers ~ POLLS
A6. xkcd creator and "What If?" author Munroe ~ RANDALL
A8. Anxious condition, briefly ~ OCD
A9. [I could sure go for some cud right now...] ~ MOO
A10. "I love" in Latin ~ AMO
A11. The fourth word of the iconic Star Wars opening text ~ AGO
A12. Dirty ___ (alliterative Spongebob character and foil to Pinhead Larry) ~ DAN
A13. Green Eggs and Ham protagonist ~ SAM
A14. Butterfly-catching tool ~ NET
A16. Low-___ (potato quality, as an img) ~ RES
A19. Some batteries ~ AAS
A21. Chinese zodiac animal ~ RAT
A23. Be careful around a hot one! ~ MIC
A25. Mike's sweet partner ~ IKE
A26. Ambient musician Brian ~ ENO
A27. Chill mentality ~ ZEN
A28. Mil. rank ~ SGT
A29. Very versatile bits of plastic ~ ZIPTIES
A31. Like a pair of Air Jordans ~ NIKES
A32. Refusals ~ NOS

D1. One "minding the gap" at the Tube ~ LONDONER
D2. Simpsons headline "___ MAN YELLS AT CLOUD" ~ OLD
D3. 2009 web series "___ With Hats" about two animals getting into hijinks ~ LLAMAS
D4. Ghost-eater, sometimes ~ PACMAN
D5. "Betcha can't eat just one", for one ~ SLOGAN
D6. Trucker anthem "King of the ___" (10-4 good buddy!) ~ ROAD
D7. What Rumpelstiltskin could have used to turn his gold straw-thread into a golden blanket ~ LOOM
D15. Orange Pekoe, e.g. ~ TEA
D17. "Totes, me too" ~ SAMESIES
D18. Make smaller, as a tailor ~ TAKEIN
D20. Lightly burns ~ SINGES
D21. What someone who can draw a Cool S probably has ~ RIZZ
D22. Big ball bowling ~ TENPIN
D24. Barracks beds ~ COTS
D30. Bout-ender, briefly ~ TKO

